# Agent rules load entry

Cursor project rules do not auto-load `.agents/rules/` as `.mdc` files. This file is the load entry: always apply root agent guidance and require reading the numbered specs under `.agents/rules/` for the task at hand.

## Canonical locations

- `@AGENTS.md` — agent entry point and constraint summary (always follow)
- `@.agents/rules/` — detailed reusable rules (`00`–`10`; start from `@.agents/rules/README.md`)
- `@.agents/templates/` — documentation / RFC / review templates
- Project-specific architecture: `@.agents/rules/10-smtgit-project-conventions.md`

## When to read which rules

| Task | Read |
|------|------|
| Any change | `AGENTS.md`; apply source-of-truth hierarchy there |
| Code / CLI / layout | `10-smtgit-project-conventions.md` |
| Docs / README | `02`, `04`, `05` |
| RFCs | `03`, `09`; use `RFCs/TEMPLATE.md` |
| Evidence / review / lifecycle | `01`, `06`, `07`, `08` |
| Authority / governance | `00`, `09` |

## Hard constraints (do not weaken)

- Human Maintainers own RFC acceptance, security/governance policy, releases, and irreversible changes.
- Pure bash + system `git`; no destructive git operations without Maintainer-approved RFC.
- Do not invent licenses, tests, security guarantees, or missing tooling.
- Prefer linking to `.agents/rules/` over copying full procedures into this rule or into `AGENTS.md`.
